+# Retry Failed Test Cases — Implementation Notes
+
+This implementation is based on Catch2 `v3.16.0` at commit
+`317ac1ed4c0bb6e6b91eafc817e05c488feffcb3`. It adds the command-line option
+`--retry-failed N`, where `N` is the number of retries after the first attempt
+and the default is zero.
+
+## 1. Execution design
+
+The parsed retry count is stored in `ConfigData` and exposed through
+`IConfig::retryFailed()`. `RunContext::runTest` keeps the existing single
+logical `testCaseStarting`/`testCaseEnded` lifetime and runs complete attempts
+inside it:
+
+1. Snapshot the current assertion totals.
+2. Emit `testCaseAttemptStarting` when retries are enabled.
+3. Call `runTestAttempt`, which performs the full tracker, section, generator,
+   fixture, output-capture, and partial-run lifecycle.
+4. Compute the attempt outcome and emit `testCaseAttemptEnded`.
+5. Stop or restore superseded assertion totals and start the next attempt.
+6. Emit one final `testCaseEnded` for the logical test case.
+
+Attempt numbers are one-based. `maxAttempts` is calculated as
+`uint64_t(N) + 1`, so the largest accepted unsigned retry count does not
+overflow. With `N == 0`, the original path is preserved: no attempt events are
+emitted, compatibility fields keep their defaults, and reporter output is
+unchanged.
+
+## 2. Retry decision and final outcome
+
+The retry decision is made only after `runTestAttempt` has completed all
+partial runs needed for section and generator traversal and has torn down the
+test case. Another attempt starts exactly when:
+
+```text
+attempt failed AND retries remain AND the test run is not aborting
+```
+
+Catch2 stops on the first non-failing attempt or after `N + 1` attempts. The
+last attempt that ran is authoritative for the logical test result, process
+exit status, and final assertion/test-case totals. A passing final attempt
+after one or more failed attempts sets `TestCaseStats::isFlaky`; an exhausted
+test remains failed. A skip is a non-failing final outcome and is not retried.
+
+## 3. State reset between attempts
+
+Each retry is a complete test-case run, not a resumed assertion or partial
+run.
+
+| State | Reset mechanism |
+| --- | --- |
+| Tracker and sections | `TrackerContext::startRun()` creates a new root for every attempt; `startCycle()` still drives each partial run. |
+| Generators | New trackers recreate generator traversal from the beginning while preserving configured generator/path filters. |
+| Fixtures | `prepareTestCase()` and `tearDownTestCase()` bracket every attempt. Persistent fixtures remain persistent only across partial runs within one attempt and are reconstructed for a retry. |
+| Randomness | `seedRng(*m_config)` runs at the start of every attempt, reproducing the configured seed while keeping generators within that attempt distinct. |
+| Captured output | Redirect buffers are drained and cleared after every partial run, accumulated per attempt, and then appended in attempt order for the logical test case. |
+| Assertions | The atomic `passed`, `failed`, `failedButOk`, and `skipped` counts are snapshotted before an attempt and restored if that attempt is superseded. |
+| Messages and sections | Existing end-of-partial-run cleanup removes unscoped messages and closes or repairs unfinished sections before a new attempt starts. |
+
+Partial-run `partNumber` values intentionally continue increasing across
+attempts; they identify partial runs, not attempts. Catch2-managed state is
+fresh, but state owned by the test is not rolled back.
+
+## 4. Intermediate diagnostics and final totals
+
+`TestCaseAttemptStats` contains one attempt's totals, captured stdout/stderr,
+abort flag, and `isFinal`. Reporters receive it before a superseded attempt's
+assertion counts are restored, so its diagnostics remain complete. The final
+`TestCaseStats` contains only the last attempt's totals, plus concatenated
+stdout/stderr from every attempt and the fields `attemptCount`, `maxAttempts`,
+and `isFlaky`. The run totals add the logical test case exactly once.
+
+Built-in reporters retain superseded diagnostics without turning them into
+final failures. Console and compact label attempts and flaky/exhausted
+outcomes; XML and JSON store attempt structures; JUnit uses `system-out`;
+SonarQube uses sanitized comments; TeamCity uses non-failing `testStdErr`;
+TAP uses diagnostic lines; Automake reports only the final logical outcome.
+Cumulative reporters keep superseded attempt trees separately from the final
+tree.
+
+## 5. Reporter API and compatibility
+
+The public reporter interface adds:
+
+- `TestCaseAttemptInfo` with `testInfo`, `attemptNumber`, and `maxAttempts`;
+- `TestCaseAttemptStats` with per-attempt totals, output, abort state, and
+  finality;
+- `testCaseAttemptStarting` and `testCaseAttemptEnded` events;
+- `attemptCount`, `maxAttempts`, and `isFlaky` on `TestCaseStats`.
+
+Attempt events surround an attempt's partial events and are nested within the
+single logical test-case event pair. `MultiReporter` forwards them in the
+existing listener-first, reporter-second order. The event methods are
+non-pure virtual no-ops, and `IConfig::retryFailed()` is non-pure with a zero
+default. Existing custom reporters, listeners, and configuration
+implementations therefore continue to compile and behave as retry-disabled
+unless they opt in to the new data.
+
+## 6. Abort options and special tags
+
+Existing outcome rules are applied before retry selection:
+
+- failed `[!mayfail]` and expected-failing `[!shouldfail]` tests are accepted
+  and are not retried;
+- an unexpected pass of `[!shouldfail]` is a failure and can be retried;
+- explicit skips are not retried;
+- fatal signals and structured exceptions balance the active attempt event,
+  but are final and follow the existing process-termination path.
+
+`--abort` and `--abortx` take precedence. An attempt that reaches the abort
+threshold is final. Counts from a failed attempt that is actually superseded
+are restored, so it does not consume the later abort budget. In particular,
+`--abort` normally prevents retrying the first failed attempt because its
+threshold is one.
+
+## 7. Main files changed
+
+- Configuration and CLI: `src/catch2/catch_config.hpp`,
+  `src/catch2/catch_config.cpp`,
+  `src/catch2/interfaces/catch_interfaces_config.hpp`,
+  `src/catch2/interfaces/catch_interfaces_config.cpp`, and
+  `src/catch2/internal/catch_commandline.cpp` define, parse, validate, and
+  expose the option.
+- Execution: `src/catch2/internal/catch_run_context.hpp` and
+  `src/catch2/internal/catch_run_context.cpp` isolate a complete attempt,
+  implement the retry loop, restore counters, and balance fatal events.
+- Reporter contract: `src/catch2/interfaces/catch_interfaces_reporter.*` and
+  `src/catch2/reporters/catch_reporter_multi.*` define and forward attempt
+  events and final retry metadata.
+- Built-in reporting: streaming/cumulative reporter bases and the console,
+  compact, XML, JSON, JUnit, SonarQube, TeamCity, and TAP reporters preserve
+  intermediate diagnostics while reporting the final outcome correctly.
+- Tests: `tests/ExtraTests/X96-RetryFailed.cpp`,
+  `tests/TestScripts/testRetryFailed.py`,
+  `tests/TestScripts/testRetryFailedFatal.py`, `tests/CMakeLists.txt`,
+  `tests/ExtraTests/CMakeLists.txt`, and focused SelfTest cases provide CLI,
+  lifecycle, state, reporter, fatal-path, and compatibility coverage.
+- Documentation: `docs/command-line.md`, `docs/reporter-events.md`,
+  `docs/reporters.md`, and `docs/test-fixtures.md` document user and extension
+  behavior.
+- Distribution: `extras/catch_amalgamated.hpp` and
+  `extras/catch_amalgamated.cpp` were regenerated with the project script.
